{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1446438-the-brain-men-of-mars-alien-abductors-for-tc-adventure","id":1446438,"title":"THE BRAIN MEN OF MARS: Alien Abductors for TC Adventure!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-29T06:06:20-07:00","id":1446438,"title":"THE BRAIN MEN OF MARS: Alien Abductors for TC Adventure!","content":"<span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hello all! Below is a creature that I intend to use as &quot;Alien Invasion&quot; goons for an upcoming Trinity Continuum: Adventure! game. I will be detailing more of such creatures, concepts and setting over at <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/brain-men-of-50587282\" target=\"_blank\">my patreon</a> in the days to come.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Brain Men of Mars were originally created by Fletcher Hanks, and first appeared in </span></span></span></span><a href=\"http://comicbookplus.com/?dlid=20882\" target=\"_blank\">Fantastic Comics #6</a><span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> (and is in the Public Domain).</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>THE BRAIN MEN OF MARS</b><br /> <img src=\"https://c10.patreonusercontent.com/3/eyJ3ZWJwIjowfQ%3D%3D/patreon-media/p/post/50587282/6f4c1d16ad3a4f798778828e1eb890ec/1.jpg?token-time=1620950400&amp;token-hash=SQQgoqr5Br_7pRHg3MlY6_fEdkFNvvSL6jW6ZJ-Wz0w%3D\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> The Brain-Men of Mars (or Skomah) are a species of aliens who have been encountered on Mars, the Moon and in remote locations on Earth. They are green-skinned, hairless humanoids who required mechanized exoskeletons to help their small bodies support the weight of their gigantic heads. The Brain Men have a high level of technology, creating everything from space-ships, mutated monsters, death rays and other wonders (see further articles for details). The Brain Men serve the mysterious &quot;Great Brains of Mars,&quot; serving their interests and fighting their battles. These aliens are coldly logical and unendingly curious about other species. Unfortunately, this curiosity takes the form of kidnapping and experimenting on animals and humans.<br /> <b>Notes: </b>The Great Brains that the Brain Men make reference to are the Doyen, who use these little monsters as &quot;crash test dummies&quot; and goons. The Brain Men are self-willed beings in their own right, but see the Doyen as gods, serving them loyally. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-------------------------------------</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>BRAIN MEN SOLDIER</b> (MEDIUM THREAT)<br /> Brain Men Soldiers are the rank and file of the Brain Men, serving as grunt troops.<br /> <b>Primary Pool:</b> 6 (Aim, Close Combat, Technology)<br /> <b>Secondary Pool:</b> 4 (Control, Larceny, Science)<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 3<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Health:</b> 4<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Hair Trigger Reflexes \u2022,Iron Will \u2022\u2022, Small Unit Tactics \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Inspiration Trait:</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022 (Destructive \u2022\u2022, Intuitive \u2022)<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Brain Jamming, Brain Skimming, Direct Voice, Telluric Resonance, Traversing the Impassable<br /> <b>Equipment Bonuses:</b> +0 Enhancement</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">POWERS AND EQUIPMENT</span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Death Ray Lance:</b> These rifles can fire a tremendous blast of heat. Attacks with this weapon have a combination of Ranged (Medium) and has the Aggravated, Incendiary and Two-Handed tags, and is of the ray damage type. If used as melee weapon, the Ray Lance acts as an edged weapon with the Quality 2, Deadly, Melee, Two-Handed tags.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Space Suit:</b> These silver, bubble helmeted suits grant the Brain Men the Beyond the Human Limit Gift (see Adventure Manuscript pt 4, page 61) as well as providing built-in armor, with the Complete, Hard 1, Soft 2, Complete, and Environmental 1 tags. If deprived of these exoskeletons, the Brain Men</span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> are considered Size 0 creatures. As such, they experience +2 Difficulty to all rolls where smaller physical size would be an issue.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Zero-G Familiarity:</b> Brain Men are more comfortable in micro-gravity environments than humans. Brain Men make zero-g maneuver rolls with a +1 Enhancement.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-------------------------------------</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>BRAIN MEN INVADER</b> (MODERATE THREAT)<br /> Invaders are the elite soldiers of the Brain Men. They are always in command of at least ten soldiers, and have access to monsters, weapons and vehicles. Invaders are remorseless torturers and murderers, seeing \u201clesser\u201d creatures (such as humans) as beneath their respect. However, they view Mesmerists and Stalwarts as superior beings akin to themselves, and will parlay with them if approached boldly.<br /> <b>Primary Pool:</b> 8 (Aim, Close Combat, Technology)<br /> <b>Secondary Pool:</b> 5 (Command, Control, Enigmas)<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 4<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Health:</b> 5<br /> <b>Edges:</b> Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022, Flash of Genius \u2022\u2022, Iron Will \u2022\u2022, Ms Fix-It \u2022\u2022, Small Unit Tactics \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Inspiration Trait:</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Destructive \u2022\u2022, Intuitive \u2022\u2022\u2022, Reflective \u2022)<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Brain Jamming, Brain Skimming, Cloak of Dread, Direct Voice, Hive Mind, Human Battery, Pain Amplification, Telluric Resonance, Three Moves Ahead, Traversing the Impassable<br /> <b>Equipment Bonuses:</b> +2 Enhancement</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">POWERS AND EQUIPMENT<br /> Death Ray Lance, Space Suit, Zero-G Familiarity</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#241E12\"><span style=\"font-family:aktiv-grotesk\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-------------------------------------</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-29-2021, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T11:55:40-07:00","id":1446470,"title":"","content":"Ooooo, space things! Not enough of them flying about these forums! I love the retro art style too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T21:32:07-07:00","id":1446908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;oq=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;aqs=chrome..69i57.18048j0j7&amp;client=ms-android-americamovil-us-revc&amp;sourceid=chrome-mobile&amp;ie=UTF-8#fpstate=ive&amp;vld=cid:ca25d0ea,vid:aTe0MjAZvMU,st:0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;oq=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;aqs=chrome..69i57.18048j0j7&amp;client=ms-android-americamovil-us-revc&amp;sourceid=chrome-mobile&amp;ie=UTF-8#fpstate=ive&amp;vld=cid:ca25d0ea,vid:aTe0MjAZvMU,st:0\" target=\"_blank\"> Google Search </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;oq=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;aqs=chrome..69i57.18048j0j7&amp;client=ms-android-americamovil-us-revc&amp;sourceid=chrome-mobile&amp;ie=UTF-8#fpstate=ive&amp;vld=cid:ca25d0ea,vid:aTe0MjAZvMU,st:0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.com/search?q=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;oq=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;aqs=chrome..69i57.18048j0j7&amp;client=ms-android-americamovil-us-revc&amp;sourceid=chrome-mobile&amp;ie=UTF-8#fpstate=ive&amp;vld=cid:ca25d0ea,vid:aTe0MjAZvMU,st:0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T05:24:32-07:00","id":1446958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1446438-the-brain-men-of-mars-alien-abductors-for-tc-adventure?p=1446908#post1446908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;oq=mars+attacks+death+music&amp;aqs=chrome..69i57.18048j0j7&amp;client=ms-android-americamovil-us-revc&amp;sourceid=chrome-mobile&amp;ie=UTF-8#fpstate=ive&amp;vld=cid:ca25d0ea,vid:aTe0MjAZvMU,st:0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.com/search?q=mars...e0MjAZvMU,st:0</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of thing. But these predate those cards by 22 years. And are in the public domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T11:23:50-07:00","id":1447009,"title":"","content":"Great work, although having read the original story, I kind of miss &quot;Dr. Martinous&quot; as a factor.<br /> <br /> Consider this little addition:<br /> <br /> A human Stalwart named Doctor Martin traveled to Mars. Maybe in a ship of his own design, perhaps by being captured by the Brain Men, possibly by having captured a Martian exploratory vessel and making the journey himself. Doctor Martin - a combat veteran turned scientist - was able to hold his own against the Brain Men for a time, before being overwhelmed. The Doyen - seeing the doctor as a dangerous but potentially useful tool - offered him power in exchange for becoming the war-master of the Brain Men. For the Brain Men had, up until that point, been a species that had conquered their world so long ago, they no longer knew how to properly fight. Doctor Martin, however, had skill in both science and war, and impressed his Martian foes with his strength and ambition. When given the offer, he agreed readily, renaming himself &quot;Dr. Martinous&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now he organizes ranks of Brain Men, training them in combat drills and directing their research towards more terrible weapons. While the &quot;Great Brains of Mars&quot; are still in charge, Martinous is the one who prosecutes their wars, acting as General. The Brain Men Invaders are the products of his training regimens. Even before his &quot;ascension&quot;, Dr. Martinous considered himself superior to regular humans, and this attitude has rubbed off on his subordinates.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, Dr. Martinous is an expendable tool of the Doyen. Nor are all the Brain Men completely loyal to their human general. Some secretly plot his downfall, waiting for a moment of weakness to justify removing him. Unbeknownst to Dr. Martinous, his position is precarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T12:22:27-07:00","id":1447019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1446438-the-brain-men-of-mars-alien-abductors-for-tc-adventure?p=1447009#post1447009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great work, although having read the original story, I kind of miss &quot;Dr. Martinous&quot; as a factor.<br /> <br /> Consider this little addition:<br /> <br /> A human Stalwart named Doctor Martin traveled to Mars. Maybe in a ship of his own design, perhaps by being captured by the Brain Men, possibly by having captured a Martian exploratory vessel and making the journey himself. Doctor Martin - a combat veteran turned scientist - was able to hold his own against the Brain Men for a time, before being overwhelmed. The Doyen - seeing the doctor as a dangerous but potentially useful tool - offered him power in exchange for becoming the war-master of the Brain Men. For the Brain Men had, up until that point, been a species that had conquered their world so long ago, they no longer knew how to properly fight. Doctor Martin, however, had skill in both science and war, and impressed his Martian foes with his strength and ambition. When given the offer, he agreed readily, renaming himself &quot;Dr. Martinous&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now he organizes ranks of Brain Men, training them in combat drills and directing their research towards more terrible weapons. While the &quot;Great Brains of Mars&quot; are still in charge, Martinous is the one who prosecutes their wars, acting as General. The Brain Men Invaders are the products of his training regimens. Even before his &quot;ascension&quot;, Dr. Martinous considered himself superior to regular humans, and this attitude has rubbed off on his subordinates.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, Dr. Martinous is an expendable tool of the Doyen. Nor are all the Brain Men completely loyal to their human general. Some secretly plot his downfall, waiting for a moment of weakness to justify removing him. Unbeknownst to Dr. Martinous, his position is precarious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Marvelous Bluecho! I also missed Dr. Martinious, but kept it open for Storytellers. But I like you addition too much to avoid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}